{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1947"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c163): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c163.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1947"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge art/architecture","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/art__architecture.json","changes":[{"field":"titleEn","old":"Landmarks in Your Pocket: Buildings on the Euro's National Sides","new":"Landmarks in Your Pocket: Buildings on Euro Coins and Notes"},{"field":"titleDe","old":"Wahrzeichen in der Hosentasche: Bauwerke auf den nationalen Seiten des Euro","new":"Wahrzeichen in der Hosentasche: Bauwerke auf Euromünzen und -scheinen"},{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",988],["+","The banknotes took the opposite route. So that no country would be favoured, the Austrian designer Robert Kalina drew imaginary buildings: each note shows one era of European architecture, with windows and gateways on the front and a bridge on the back. The 5-euro note stands for Classical antiquity, the 10-euro note for the Romanesque, with a round-arched stone bridge, followed by Gothic, Renaissance, Baroque and Rococo, the age of iron and glass, and modern architecture on the 500. None of the bridges existed – until the Dutch town of Spijkenisse built copies of all seven in 2013.\n\n"],["=",39]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",876],["+","Die Banknoten gingen den umgekehrten Weg. Damit kein Land bevorzugt würde, zeichnete der österreichische Gestalter Robert Kalina erfundene Bauwerke: Jeder Schein zeigt eine Epoche der europäischen Baukunst, vorne mit Fenstern und Toren, hinten mit einer Brücke. Der 5-Euro-Schein steht für die Antike, der 10-Euro-Schein für die Romanik mit einer rundbogigen Steinbrücke, es folgen Gotik, Renaissance, Barock und Rokoko, das Zeitalter von Eisen und Glas und auf dem 500er die moderne Architektur. Keine der Brücken existierte – bis die niederländische Stadt Spijkenisse 2013 Nachbildungen aller sieben baute.\n\n"],["=",33]]}]},
